{"id":"9ab4158d0f08e490","group":"58","path":"58/batch16/58-df-zfc-silver-indiscernible.md","title":"ZFC Silver Indiscernible","display":"df-zfc-silver-indiscernible — ZFC Silver Indiscernible","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-zfc-silver-indiscernible","aliases":["58-df-zfc-silver-indiscernible"],"display":"df-zfc-silver-indiscernible — ZFC Silver Indiscernible","depends_on":["[[58-ax-zfc]]","[[58-df-class]]","[[58-df-ordclass]]","[[58-df-formula]]","[[58-df-free-variable]]","[[58-df-constructible-universe]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-zfc-silver-indiscernible"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-zfc-silver-indiscernible</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-zfc-silver-indiscernible — ZFC Silver Indiscernible"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"a3348ed9eb6fb4e3\" href=\"?note=a3348ed9eb6fb4e3\" title=\"58-ax-zfc\">58-ax-zfc</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"ca2a9c9166fa8cce\" href=\"?note=ca2a9c9166fa8cce\" title=\"58-df-class\">58-df-class</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"1d8adfba370086ed\" href=\"?note=1d8adfba370086ed\" title=\"58-df-ordclass\">58-df-ordclass</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"65418b505fc53093\" href=\"?note=65418b505fc53093\" title=\"58-df-formula\">58-df-formula</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"715a32e91161b34f\" href=\"?note=715a32e91161b34f\" title=\"58-df-free-variable\">58-df-free-variable</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"de47935b5769dd1e\" href=\"?note=de47935b5769dd1e\" title=\"58-df-constructible-universe\">58-df-constructible-universe</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"I\">\\(I\\)</span> (class parameter) and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"V\">\\(V\\)</span> (von Neumann universe)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L\">\\(L\\)</span> (the fixed constructible-universe class defined in <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"de47935b5769dd1e\" href=\"?note=de47935b5769dd1e\" title=\"58-df-constructible-universe\">58-df-constructible-universe</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal L_\\in\">\\(\\mathcal L_\\in\\)</span> (the first-order language of set theory)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{PropClass}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{PropClass}_S\\)</span> (proper-class predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-8\" data-note=\"ca2a9c9166fa8cce\" href=\"?note=ca2a9c9166fa8cce\" title=\"58-df-class\">58-df-class</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Ord}\">\\(\\mathrm{Ord}\\)</span> (the ordinal class, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-9\" data-note=\"1d8adfba370086ed\" href=\"?note=1d8adfba370086ed\" title=\"58-df-ordclass\">58-df-ordclass</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\mathcal L_\\in)\">\\(\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\mathcal L_\\in)\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{FV}_{\\mathcal L_\\in}\">\\(\\operatorname{FV}_{\\mathcal L_\\in}\\)</span> (formulas and their free-variable operator)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"(L,\\in)\\models_{\\mathsf{meta}}\\varphi[\\bar\\alpha]\">\\((L,\\in)\\models_{\\mathsf{meta}}\\varphi[\\bar\\alpha]\\)</span> (metatheoretic satisfaction for the proper-class structure <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"(L,\\in)\">\\((L,\\in)\\)</span>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n\\in\\omega\">\\(n\\in\\omega\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\bar\\alpha\\in V^n\">\\(\\bar\\alpha\\in V^n\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Inc}_I^n(\\bar\\alpha)\">\\(\\mathrm{Inc}_I^n(\\bar\\alpha)\\)</span> (the increasing-tuple predicate defined here)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{SilverIndiscernibles}_S,\\mathrm{SilverIndiscernible}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{SilverIndiscernibles}_S,\\mathrm{SilverIndiscernible}_S\\)</span> (alias predicates defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}silver\\text{-}indiscernible}\\vdash_{\\mathsf{meta}}\\mathrm{SilverIndiscernibles}_S(I)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{PropClass}_S(I)\\land\\forall\\alpha\\in V\\;(\\alpha\\in I\\rightarrow\\alpha\\in\\mathrm{Ord})\\land\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;\\forall\\varphi\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\mathcal L_\\in)\\;\\Bigl(\\operatorname{FV}_{\\mathcal L_\\in}(\\varphi)\\subseteq\\{v_i:i\\in n\\}\\rightarrow\\forall\\bar\\alpha,\\bar\\beta\\in V^n\\;\\bigl(\\mathrm{Inc}_I^n(\\bar\\alpha)\\land\\mathrm{Inc}_I^n(\\bar\\beta)\\rightarrow((L,\\in)\\models_{\\mathsf{meta}}\\varphi[\\bar\\alpha]\\leftrightarrow(L,\\in)\\models_{\\mathsf{meta}}\\varphi[\\bar\\beta])\\bigr)\\Bigr),\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}silver\\text{-}indiscernible}\\vdash_{\\mathsf{meta}}\\mathrm{SilverIndiscernibles}_S(I)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{PropClass}_S(I)\\land\\forall\\alpha\\in V\\;(\\alpha\\in I\\rightarrow\\alpha\\in\\mathrm{Ord})\\land\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;\\forall\\varphi\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\mathcal L_\\in)\\;\\Bigl(\\operatorname{FV}_{\\mathcal L_\\in}(\\varphi)\\subseteq\\{v_i:i\\in n\\}\\rightarrow\\forall\\bar\\alpha,\\bar\\beta\\in V^n\\;\\bigl(\\mathrm{Inc}_I^n(\\bar\\alpha)\\land\\mathrm{Inc}_I^n(\\bar\\beta)\\rightarrow((L,\\in)\\models_{\\mathsf{meta}}\\varphi[\\bar\\alpha]\\leftrightarrow(L,\\in)\\models_{\\mathsf{meta}}\\varphi[\\bar\\beta])\\bigr)\\Bigr),\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}silver\\text{-}indiscernible\\text{-}increasing}\\vdash\\mathrm{Inc}_I^n(\\bar\\alpha)\\leftrightarrow\\bigl(\\forall i\\in n\\;(\\alpha_i\\in I)\\bigr)\\land\\bigl(\\forall i,j\\in n\\;(i\\in j\\rightarrow\\alpha_i\\in\\alpha_j)\\bigr).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}silver\\text{-}indiscernible\\text{-}increasing}\\vdash\\mathrm{Inc}_I^n(\\bar\\alpha)\\leftrightarrow\\bigl(\\forall i\\in n\\;(\\alpha_i\\in I)\\bigr)\\land\\bigl(\\forall i,j\\in n\\;(i\\in j\\rightarrow\\alpha_i\\in\\alpha_j)\\bigr).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}silver\\text{-}indiscernible\\text{-}alias}\\vdash_{\\mathsf{meta}}\\mathrm{SilverIndiscernible}_S(I)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{SilverIndiscernibles}_S(I).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}silver\\text{-}indiscernible\\text{-}alias}\\vdash_{\\mathsf{meta}}\\mathrm{SilverIndiscernible}_S(I)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{SilverIndiscernibles}_S(I).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>This atom defines the proper class of Silver indiscernibles as order indiscernibles for <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"(L,\\in)\">\\((L,\\in)\\)</span>; it does not assert that such a class exists.</li>\n<li>The fixed symbol <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L\">\\(L\\)</span> comes from <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-10\" data-note=\"de47935b5769dd1e\" href=\"?note=de47935b5769dd1e\" title=\"58-df-constructible-universe\">58-df-constructible-universe</a>. Because <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L\">\\(L\\)</span> is a proper class, its satisfaction relation is explicitly metatheoretic rather than the set-coded relation from <code>df-satisfaction</code>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Inc}_I^n\">\\(\\mathrm{Inc}_I^n\\)</span> expands the former undefined notation <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"[I]^n_\\uparrow\">\\([I]^n_\\uparrow\\)</span> into a set-coded <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n\">\\(n\\)</span>-tuple whose entries lie in <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"I\">\\(I\\)</span> and increase in the ordinal membership order.</li>\n<li>The singular symbol is retained only as a compatibility alias. Existence is the substantive principle connected with <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"0^\\sharp\">\\(0^\\sharp\\)</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-ax-zfc","status":"resolved","id":"a3348ed9eb6fb4e3","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-ax-zfc]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-class","status":"resolved","id":"ca2a9c9166fa8cce","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-class]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-ordclass","status":"resolved","id":"1d8adfba370086ed","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-ordclass]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-formula","status":"resolved","id":"65418b505fc53093","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-formula]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-free-variable","status":"resolved","id":"715a32e91161b34f","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-free-variable]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-constructible-universe","status":"resolved","id":"de47935b5769dd1e","anchor":"ref-6","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-constructible-universe]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-constructible-universe","status":"resolved","id":"de47935b5769dd1e","anchor":"ref-7","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$L$ (the fixed constructible-universe class defined in [[58-df-constructible-universe]])","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-class","status":"resolved","id":"ca2a9c9166fa8cce","anchor":"ref-8","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{PropClass}_S$ (proper-class predicate, see [[58-df-class]])","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-ordclass","status":"resolved","id":"1d8adfba370086ed","anchor":"ref-9","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Ord}$ (the ordinal class, see [[58-df-ordclass]])","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-constructible-universe","status":"resolved","id":"de47935b5769dd1e","anchor":"ref-10","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Remark]","excerpt":"The fixed symbol $L$ comes from [[58-df-constructible-universe]]. Because $L$ is a proper class, its satisfaction relation is explicitly metatheoretic rather than the set-coded relation from `df-satisfaction`.","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"I","display":false},{"tex":"V","display":false},{"tex":"L","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathcal L_\\in","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{PropClass}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Ord}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\mathcal L_\\in)","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{FV}_{\\mathcal L_\\in}","display":false},{"tex":"(L,\\in)\\models_{\\mathsf{meta}}\\varphi[\\bar\\alpha]","display":false},{"tex":"(L,\\in)","display":false},{"tex":"n\\in\\omega","display":false},{"tex":"\\bar\\alpha\\in V^n","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Inc}_I^n(\\bar\\alpha)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{SilverIndiscernibles}_S,\\mathrm{SilverIndiscernible}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}silver\\text{-}indiscernible}\\vdash_{\\mathsf{meta}}\\mathrm{SilverIndiscernibles}_S(I)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{PropClass}_S(I)\\land\\forall\\alpha\\in V\\;(\\alpha\\in I\\rightarrow\\alpha\\in\\mathrm{Ord})\\land\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;\\forall\\varphi\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\mathcal L_\\in)\\;\\Bigl(\\operatorname{FV}_{\\mathcal L_\\in}(\\varphi)\\subseteq\\{v_i:i\\in n\\}\\rightarrow\\forall\\bar\\alpha,\\bar\\beta\\in V^n\\;\\bigl(\\mathrm{Inc}_I^n(\\bar\\alpha)\\land\\mathrm{Inc}_I^n(\\bar\\beta)\\rightarrow((L,\\in)\\models_{\\mathsf{meta}}\\varphi[\\bar\\alpha]\\leftrightarrow(L,\\in)\\models_{\\mathsf{meta}}\\varphi[\\bar\\beta])\\bigr)\\Bigr),","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}silver\\text{-}indiscernible\\text{-}increasing}\\vdash\\mathrm{Inc}_I^n(\\bar\\alpha)\\leftrightarrow\\bigl(\\forall i\\in n\\;(\\alpha_i\\in I)\\bigr)\\land\\bigl(\\forall i,j\\in n\\;(i\\in j\\rightarrow\\alpha_i\\in\\alpha_j)\\bigr).","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}silver\\text{-}indiscernible\\text{-}alias}\\vdash_{\\mathsf{meta}}\\mathrm{SilverIndiscernible}_S(I)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{SilverIndiscernibles}_S(I).","display":true},{"tex":"(L,\\in)","display":false},{"tex":"L","display":false},{"tex":"L","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Inc}_I^n","display":false},{"tex":"[I]^n_\\uparrow","display":false},{"tex":"n","display":false},{"tex":"I","display":false},{"tex":"0^\\sharp","display":false}],"bytes":2998,"backlinks":[{"id":"94c497a695780952","anchor":"ref-6","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""},{"id":"06c9bb13a5d511e9","anchor":"ref-4","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$\\mathrm{SilverIndiscernibles}_S(I)$ 表示类 $I$ 是 $L$ 的 Silver 不可辨识元类（see [[../batch16/58-df-zfc-silver-indiscernible.md]]）；$I$ 在类元理论中取值。"},{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-3489","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch16/58-df-zfc-silver-indiscernible.md|5